DESCRIPTION Discovery band, list nodes with roles/capacity/Ready condition; real node identities, no invented nodes.

DEFINE CONST TIERS AS "standard"
DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "List the Kubernetes nodes with their roles, CPU and memory capacity, and
  current Ready condition."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "node")

# Reference-grounded quality, deferred LLM judge (FitnessCrew) scores the
# synthesis 0.0-1.0 against this ground truth from cluster-ground-truth-baseline.md.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The correct answer is the node list the Kubernetes API shows at the time of the question, so grade it against the live nodes and not against an assumed all-Ready cluster. A correct answer lists every node (all named homelab-k8s-..., control-plane, gpu-worker and worker nodes), gives the total count, and gives each node's role, CPU and memory capacity and current Ready condition exactly as the live data shows. A node that is NotReady or cordoned (SchedulingDisabled) is correctly reported with that state, not omitted and not reported as Ready. Reporting only a couple of nodes or leaving out capacity is a severe under-report. A node name that is not in the cluster, a count that does not match the live count, a Ready status that contradicts the live condition, or a capacity figure that does not match the node's live capacity is fabrication and fails the answer.")
